(kmotion_m6: M6 on the KMotion board. The ini remaps M6 here - [RS274NGC] REMAP=M6 modalgroup=6 ngc=kmotion_m6,)
(SUBROUTINE_PATH = ../../ngc - and this runs the board's tool change program: M198 is the mcodes/M198 wrapper, which)
(sends the selected pocket and tool ID to kmotion-motion, which runs [KMOTION] TOOL_CHANGE with them in its)
(persist variable and the next one as ints, KMotionCNC's M6 convention, and waits for the program. Then LinuxCNC)
(is told the tool is in the spindle. The tool's offsets - length, and X and Y on a machine with a spindle per)
(tool - are G43's business in LinuxCNC and stay those of the last G43 through an M6. With [KMOTION])
(TOOL_LENGTH_IMMEDIATELY = 1 the new tool's offsets apply here, as KMotionCNC's Tool Length Immediately does:)
(a T1 M6 from MDI or the GUI's button then leaves no other tool's offsets in force - which a home program's)
(set-DRO, G10 L20, would fold into the fixture offset.)
(The offsets are asked for by the tool's number, G43 H, not as "the tool in the spindle": that holds whether or)
(not the interpreter has taken the change in yet. T0, the unload, cancels them: G49.)
o<kmotion_m6> sub
#<tool> = #<_selected_tool>
M198 P#<_selected_pocket> Q#<tool>
M61 Q#<tool>
o100 if [EXISTS[#<_ini[KMOTION]TOOL_LENGTH_IMMEDIATELY>]]
  o110 if [#<_ini[KMOTION]TOOL_LENGTH_IMMEDIATELY> NE 0]
    o120 if [#<tool> GT 0]
      G43 H#<tool>
    o120 else
      G49
    o120 endif
  o110 endif
o100 endif
o<kmotion_m6> endsub
M2
